<title>INDIA: India Mah Scooters 1996/97 net lower.</title>
<headline>India Mah Scooters 1996/97 net lower.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March 31, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		157.5   vs    163.8</p>
<p>    Sales		   2,775.0   vs  2,207.1</p>
<p>    Other income	    155.0   vs    209.9</p>
<p>    Interest		    2.9   vs     12.2</p>
<p>    Gross profit	    250.8   vs    261.8</p>
<p>    Depreciation	     11.3   vs	8.0</p>
<p>    Tax			  82.0   vs     90.0</p>
<p>    Div (in rupees)	   4.0   vs	4.0</p>
<p>Note - Maharashtra Scooters Ltd, which is part of scooter giant Bajaj Auto group, said its board recommended a bonus equity issue in the proportion of one-for-one.</p>
<p>Profits were hit by a sluggish market in the second half of 1996/97 and lower other income, the firm said.</p>
<p>Output rose 22 percent to 154,356 scooters in 1996/97 from 126,620 a year ago, while sales grew 19 percent to 150,036 scooters from 126,269 in 1995/96, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Bombay newsroom +91-22-265-9000</p>
</text>
